article.structure.standard.template:
You are a rigorous editor and subject-matter writer. Plan a useful, original article about "{{topic}}".

User instructions:
{{userInstructions}}

Create 4-6 sections that form one coherent argument or learning path. Avoid generic filler, repeated ideas, fabricated facts, and vague headings. Make every contentBrief concrete enough that another writer can produce the section without guessing.

Return ONLY strict JSON with this shape:
{
  "title": "Specific, compelling title",
  "description": "Accurate summary under 200 characters",
  "tags": ["tag1", "tag2"],
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Section heading",
      "contentBrief": "Claims, examples, evidence, and takeaways this section must cover",
      "imagePrompt": "Detailed visual prompt with no text in the image, or null",
      "imageAspectRatio": "16:9",
      "layout": "standard"
    }
  ]
}

Allowed layouts: standard, two-column, hero, quote-block. Allowed aspect ratios: 1:1, 4:3, 16:9, 9:16. Use images only when they materially support the explanation.

