book.page.structure.template:
You are an expert co-author and researcher. Plan a comprehensive book page about "{{topic}}" as a natural continuation of this conversation:

{{history}}

Preserve the user's distinctive reasoning while improving clarity and structure. Return ONLY strict JSON with a title and sections array. Every section must contain heading, contentBrief, imagePrompt or null, imageAspectRatio, and layout. Allowed layouts: standard, two-column, hero, quote-block. Allowed aspect ratios: 1:1, 4:3, 16:9, 9:16.

book.page.content.template:
You are an expert co-author. Write a substantial book page that preserves the insights and reasoning in the conversation.

Title: {{title}}
Conversation:
{{history}}

Planned sections:
{{sectionsJson}}

Available image URLs by heading:
{{imageUrlsJson}}

Return ONLY semantic HTML suitable inside an <article>. Each substantial section should contain 250-500 useful words without padding. Use concrete examples and accurate explanations. Never invent facts, quotations, or sources. Use supplied images only for matching headings and never fabricate URLs. Tailwind-compatible typography classes are allowed, but do not set section or container background colors. Do not return markdown, <html>, <head>, or <body>.

social.linkedin.template:
Write a professional, engaging LinkedIn post announcing a new {{type}}.

Title: {{title}}
Description: {{description}}

Open with a specific hook, explain the reader value, use a professional conversational voice, and include 2-3 genuinely relevant hashtags. Keep the complete post under 1,000 characters. Do not include a link. Return only the post text.

social.linkedin.rich.template:
Create a professional LinkedIn post plan for a newly published {{type}}.

Title: {{title}}
Description: {{description}}
Requested format: {{format}}

Return ONLY strict JSON with this shape:
{
  "format": "{{format}}",
  "commentary": "Complete LinkedIn caption under 1,000 characters",
  "imageAltText": "Meaningful description when the format is image",
  "hashtags": ["RelevantTag"],
  "slides": [
    {
      "headline": "Short slide headline, maximum 8 words",
      "body": "One focused idea in 15-40 words",
      "altText": "Accessible description of the slide",
      "imagePrompt": "A concrete visual concept supporting this slide, with no text in the image"
    }
  ]
}

Open the commentary with a specific hook, explain concrete reader value, end with a natural call to action, and include 2-3 genuinely relevant hashtags. Do not include a link. For document format, create 5-8 slides that form a coherent sequence: strong cover, focused insights, and a closing takeaway. Give every document slide a distinct imagePrompt that illustrates its specific idea without repeating the headline as typography. For text or image format, return an empty slides array. Avoid generic motivational language, fabricated claims, and repeated ideas.

social.linkedin.image.template:
Create a premium editorial portrait image for a LinkedIn post about this newly published {{type}}.

Title: {{title}}
Description: {{description}}

Translate the central idea into one memorable visual metaphor with a clear focal subject, sophisticated composition, strong depth, restrained color, and polished studio or cinematic lighting. It should feel credible in a professional feed, not like generic corporate stock art. Use the full 4:5 canvas and leave comfortable visual breathing room. Do not include text, typography, letters, numbers, logos, watermarks, screenshots, interface elements, or LinkedIn branding.

social.linkedin.slide-image.template:
